# goal A self-contained public distribution surface

`sites/git-a2a.com/` is the complete static package served at `https://git-a2a.com`: product
documentation, public schemas, the A2A extension description, and checksum-verifying installers.

# decision Site publication is automated but separate from CLI releases {#publication}

Pushes to `main` that change the static site or its canonical inputs run the dedicated site
workflow after `make site-check`; CLI tags and the release workflow never deploy the site. The
workflow stages an explicit allowlist through `scripts/site-package.sh` and uploads that staging
directory with OpenSSH. Hosting account, endpoint, port, document root, private key, and host-key
material exist only as protected `site-production` environment secrets; workflow source and logs
must not reveal their values. Design sources, generators, operator documentation, and repository
metadata are never part of the upload.

Manual publication uses `make site-publish`, the same allowlist, and local OpenSSH. Its endpoint,
account, document root, and optional SSH paths come from the gitignored root `.env`; only an empty
`.env.example` is tracked. Manual publication must pass `site-check` before contacting the host.

# invariant Canonical files stay byte-identical {#canonical_files}

The public `install.sh` is byte-identical to the repository-root `install.sh` used by release
documentation. `schema/a2amodule.v1.json` and `schema/a2amodule-lock.v1.json` are byte-identical
to their respective files under `spec/schema/`. Checks fail on drift.

# decision Static, local-first implementation {#static_site}

The site uses hand-written HTML and one CSS and JavaScript file, with no framework, generator,
analytics, remote fonts, or runtime service. Every page renders from `file://` and an ordinary
static HTTP server. The only JavaScript behaviours are transcript replay, copy buttons, and
keyboard-accessible install tabs.

# decision Visual source and static asset provenance {#visual_source}

`sites/design/README.md` is authoritative for copy, tokens, spacing, typography, and behaviour;
its prototypes are references, never production markup. IBM Plex Sans and JetBrains Mono are
pinned OFL WOFF2 assets. Wordmark glyphs are outlined by the committed CoreText generator,
size-specific favicons by ImageMagick, and social cards by the committed headless-Chrome template.

# invariant The transcript is real and accessible {#transcript}

`assets/transcript.json` contains trimmed real 1.0.0 CLI output from local acme bare repositories.
The landing embeds identical completed data as its no-JavaScript and `file://` fallback. Reduced
motion skips typing, replay clears every timer, and the terminal copy action returns only the four
commands.

# build Site and installer checks

`make installers-check` parses and dry-runs the POSIX installer without network access. The
complete site gate is `make site-check`; it verifies synced files, HTML and links, duplicated
header/footer bytes, content policy, and the transfer budget.
